## Highest-Risk Bug: Partial Batch Persistence

**Location:** `src/main/java/com/example/importer/UserImportService.java`, lines 16-20

**Root Cause:** Rows are persisted **immediately during iteration** before the entire batch is validated. If validation fails on row N, rows 1 through N-1 are already committed to the database with no rollback.

```java
for (UserRow row : rows) {
    if (row.getEmail() == null || row.getEmail().isBlank()) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("email required");
    }
    userRepository.insert(row.getEmail(), row.getDisplayName());  // ❌ Insert happens BEFORE full batch validation
}
```

---

## Smallest Safe Fix

**File:** `src/main/java/com/example/importer/UserImportService.java`

**Change:** Separate validation from insertion. Validate all rows first, then insert only if all pass.

```java
public void importCsv(String csvText) {
    List<UserRow> rows = csvParser.parse(csvText);

    // Validate all rows first
    for (UserRow row : rows) {
        if (row.getEmail() == null || row.getEmail().isBlank()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("email required");
        }
    }

    // Insert all rows only after validation passes
    for (UserRow row : rows) {
        userRepository.insert(row.getEmail(), row.getDisplayName());
    }
}
```

---

## Regression Checks

| Test Case | Expected Behavior |
|-----------|-------------------|
| All rows valid | All rows inserted |
| One row invalid (email null/blank) | **Zero rows** inserted, exception thrown |
| Empty CSV | No inserts, no exception |
| Multiple invalid rows | Zero rows inserted, exception on first invalid |

---

## Note on Transaction Support

If `UserRepository` supports transactions, consider wrapping the second loop in a transaction for additional safety. However, the above fix alone prevents partial persistence by design.
